lenses.summary:
AA-Booking can be AI-first for sales, ops and pricing, but today it has no AI to build on. It is a live health-only slice (bk-001; the slice-2 inquiry-intake worktree is still empty), has no LLM access path and no pricing tables. ADR 0005 already defines a deterministic pricing model: net rates per contract, a cost sheet per pax band and season, selling price = net / (1 - margin), floors, and FX locked when a quote is sent. That model should stay the only thing that produces numbers.

The design rule for this lens: **AI extracts, maps and drafts. Deterministic code computes and checks every price. A named human publishes or sends.** This follows the patterns CIS has already proven:
- the a0_column_map "static map first, LLM fallback" mapper;
- validate stages on a different vendor (ADR 0008);
- the number-grounding check in grounding.py;
- Jev typed questions in shadow mode before enforce;
- fail-closed brand audit;
- llm_call_log cost rows on every model call.

I propose 13 use-cases.

**Start with these (low risk, high leverage):**
- an anomaly brief for rate uploads before publish;
- a quote integrity and margin guard;
- the price_raw reference-price parse;
- inquiry triage with a first-reply draft.

**Then the high-value, high-risk extraction and drafting work:** supplier PDF and email rate extraction under maker-checker, cost-sheet drafts from CIS tour days, V1..Vn version drafting, and supplier booking emails.

**Blocking prerequisites, all missing today:**
- an LLM path for Booking: its task role has no Bedrock, the satellites trust only the CIS task role, it has no llm_call_log grant, and the gateway exists only as CIS and TripPlanner copies;
- the booking.job worker;
- bk-00x rate, FX, pricing-rule and cost-sheet migrations, and the staff contracting role;
- an email channel;
- a safe file-upload path, because REST API Gateway corrupts binary uploads;
- an inquiry contract that carries dates, pax, budget and language;
- an explicit policy on supplier-document prompt injection and on which providers may see customer PII.

current_state:
ADR 0005 sets the pricing rules:
- all supplier, rate, FX, pricing-rule, cost-sheet and quote data lives in schema booking;
- new rates are new rows with new validity, never overwrites;
- cost sheet per pax band (1, 2, 3-4, 5-6, 7-10, 11+) × season;
- selling price = net / (1 - margin); B2C tailor-made target 30%, floor 20%; B2B 15%, floor 10%;
- an override below the floor needs a reason and is audited;
- base currency USD; FX is locked when a quote is sent; quotes are valid 7-14 days;
- Phase 1 loading = Excel template → validation → staff review → versioned publish.
(docs/adr/0005-pricing-and-supplier-rates.md:19-54)
The root-adr worktree diff marks ADR 0005 Accepted and adds decision 8 (contracting role, maker-checker, one sheet per service type), 9 (tenant B2B resale with rate parity) and 10 (tax_rules table, rates still with the accountant).

ERD v2 target model (docs/AAA/erd-v2/booking.dbml):
- trip_case_status runs new_inquiry → discovery → building → proposal_sent → confirmed → supplier_confirming → … → completed (:29-43);
- trip_case_versions has total_price, currency, is_sent_to_customer and is_approved, with at most one approved version (:384-401);
- version itinerary lines carry unit_price (:403-418);
- supplier_bookings has price, voucher, confirmation_ref and status (:445-460);
- payments keep a receipt as evidence_media_id (:532-533).
No FX-rate, net-cost, margin or rate-provenance columns exist on versions or lines.

The CIS Model Gateway is the platform AI layer:
- every call goes through LLMClient.generate(stage=...), and a unit test blocks raw Bedrock/OpenAI calls (apps/AA-CIS-App/CONTEXT.md:101-107);
- model routes are DB-driven via shared.llm_role_config and llm_model_catalog, with fallback and shadow (:84-100);
- writers are Anthropic and judges use a different vendor; validate/extraction stages may use any vendor (apps/AA-CIS-App/docs/adr/0008-validate-stages-any-vendor.md:18-24);
- the cost guard shared.spend_budget only covers guarded CIS jobs (CONTEXT.md:148-154).

Reusable guardrails in CIS:
- grounding.py flags any number in generated text that is absent from the cited source, with 0 false positives on 79 real units (apps/AA-CIS-App/services/acp_shared/grounding.py:15-24);
- brand audit fails closed to manual_check (CONTEXT.md:97-98);
- prompt_sanitize.py is only 'self-injection containment' for a tenant's own text, not general defense (apps/AA-CIS-App/shared/validators/prompt_sanitize.py:12-14).

Booking cannot call an LLM today:
- its task role grants SSM only, with 'No Bedrock, no S3' (infra/AA-CIS-Infra/accounts/aa365/booking.tf:207-238);
- the Bedrock satellite roles trust only the CIS ECS task role (apps/AA-CIS-App/CONTEXT.md:80-83; infra/AA-CIS-Infra/accounts/aa365/bedrock_satellite_assume.tf:20-40);
- ADR 0004 gives Booking no llm_call_log grant until it calls an LLM (docs/adr/0004-aa-booking-stack-and-bootstrap.md:158-159);
- TripPlanner runs its own gateway copy at backend/shared/llm_gateway.py (apps/AA-TripPlanner-Web/CONTEXT.md:133-145).

CIS does not hold a structured day→service model (hotel night, vehicle-day, guide-day, entrance fee):
- tour_atoms are place/action/activity_type moments (docs/architecture/db-schema-reference.md:190-214);
- raw_tours inclusions and exclusions are free text (:267-268);
- TripPlanner itinerary_components hold activity/name/destination per source day (:1507-1520).

Constraints from the lessons log (skill/aa-lessons/lessons.md):
- binary uploads through a REST API Gateway without binaryMediaTypes get corrupted (:41);
- an enrichment A/B must include other vendors (:56);
- a fact judge must see the source and name each claim (:79);
- cost and volume numbers must come from real queries (:21).
The eval-regression workflow is on-demand only and covers s1_old (apps/AA-CIS-App/.github/workflows/eval-regression.yml:1-6, 18-20).

opportunities.what_ai_does:
Extracts net rates from supplier contract PDFs, scanned rate cards and email bodies (hotel room type × season × meal plan, single supplement, extra bed; vehicle-day; guide language/day; entrance adult/child; activity per pax or group) into template rows. Every value carries a source citation (page or cell plus a quoted snippet). Deterministic validators then run:
- ISO currency;
- valid_from < valid_to;
- unit enum;
- net > 0;
- no overlap with existing contract rows;
- every number must appear verbatim in the cited snippet (reusing the grounding.py idea).
This runs as a validate stage (any vendor, ADR 0008) as a bk_rate_extract job.

Deterministic diffs against the currently valid contract:
- percentage change per row;
- missing seasons or pax bands;
- validity gaps;
- a currency switched against history;
- outliers against other suppliers of the same service type and destination;
- rates expiring before already-quoted travel dates.
A cheap LLM then writes a short brief listing what to look at first. It explains the computed facts and never changes or adds a number.

Rule checks, mostly deterministic:
- margin below the channel floor;
- peak uplift missing for Tết or festival dates;
- a rate expired before the travel date;
- the wrong pax band for the group size;
- stale FX;
- total ≠ sum of lines;
- a B2B tenant retail price below AA's public 'from' price (rate parity).
The LLM drafts the plain-language explanation and pre-fills the override-reason form; it never decides.

gaps:
Booking has no LLM path:
- its task role has no Bedrock or S3 access (infra/AA-CIS-Infra/accounts/aa365/booking.tf:207-210);
- the satellite invoker roles trust only the CIS ECS task role (apps/AA-CIS-App/CONTEXT.md:80-83);
- there is no llm_call_log grant (docs/adr/0004-aa-booking-stack-and-bootstrap.md:158-159);
- the gateway lives as a CIS module and a TripPlanner copy (apps/AA-TripPlanner-Web/CONTEXT.md:133-145), so a third copy is likely.
Decision needed: package the gateway as one shared library (as ADR 0003 decision 4 did for jobs), register bk_* stages in llm_role_config, and add a CIS migration granting role booking SELECT on config and INSERT on llm_call_log.

There is no general prompt-injection policy for third-party text. prompt_sanitize.py states it is only self-injection containment (apps/AA-CIS-App/shared/validators/prompt_sanitize.py:12-14). Supplier PDFs, emails and customer messages need an architectural rule:
- extraction stages output a strict schema only, with no tools;
- document text never selects actions, recipients or prices;
- every extracted number must be grounded verbatim in the source;
- outbound actions always need a human click.
